    <string name="settings_phantom_title">Android child-process limits</string>
    <string name="settings_phantom_desc">On Android 12 and newer the system can pause or kill extra processes TermFold starts (same as Termux). Agent chats may hold a CPU wake lock while they are working. Terminals never wake-lock on their own: use Wake and Auto on the terminal key row (Wake off by default; Auto on keeps the lock only while output is flowing; Auto off keeps it until you turn Wake off). Wi‑Fi also uses a radio lock when a wake lock is active. If work still stalls with the screen off, allow unrestricted battery, then try Developer options → disable child process restrictions.</string>
